      *>--- conformance-case
      *> id: g85_bf03_09
      *> rules: [1985-GR-IV.4.2.2.2.3-6]
      *> accept: [85]
      *> source-format: fixed
      *> portable: unverified
      *>---
      *> §1985:IV.4.2.2.2.3 GR6 - ALL literal represents all or part of
      *> the string generated by successive concatenations of the
      *> characters of the literal; its length comes from context
      *> (the paragraph's length rules (1) and (3)). ALL "AB" to X(5)
      *> is ABABA, VALUE ALL "XYZ" on X(4) is XYZX, ALL "ABCD" to X(2)
      *> is AB (truncated from the right), a comparison with ALL "AB"
      *> repeats it to the item's size, and DISPLAY ALL "QZ" (not
      *> associated with an item) is the literal once. A compiler that
      *> padded with spaces or kept one copy fails a line.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. G85BF0309.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  X5 PIC X(5).
       01  X4 PIC X(4) VALUE ALL "XYZ".
       01  X2 PIC X(2).
       01  C6 PIC X(6) VALUE "ABABAB".
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       P1.
           MOVE ALL "AB" TO X5.
           DISPLAY "X5=[" X5 "]".
           DISPLAY "X4=[" X4 "]".
           MOVE ALL "ABCD" TO X2.
           DISPLAY "X2=[" X2 "]".
           IF C6 = ALL "AB"
               DISPLAY "C6-EQ"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "C6-NE".
           IF X5 = ALL "AB"
               DISPLAY "X5-EQ"
           ELSE
               DISPLAY "X5-NE".
           DISPLAY "D=[" ALL "QZ" "]".
           STOP RUN.
